    "Register your interest": "登记您的意向",
    "Why the summit is at KICC, and why the expo is in a tent": "为什么峰会在KICC举行,为什么博览会在帐篷内举行",
    "The venue is confirmed. Here is how the three days use it.": "场地已确认。以下是三天活动的使用安排。",
    "The Kenya-China Tea Summit runs at the Kenyatta International Convention Centre\non Harambee Avenue, in the middle of Nairobi's central business district.": "Kenya-China Tea Summit在位于Nairobi中央商务区中心Harambee Avenue的Kenyatta International Convention Centre举行。",
    "The building": "建筑",
    "KICC sits within walking distance of the government quarter, the main hotel\ncluster and Uhuru Park. For a delegation arriving from outside Kenya that\nmatters more than it sounds: a venue at the edge of a city turns every\nbetween-session conversation into a taxi journey, and the conversations\nbetween sessions are most of what a trade summit is for.": "KICC位于政府区、主要酒店群和Uhuru Park的步行距离内。对于从肯尼亚境外抵达的代表团而言,这一点比听起来更重要:位于城市边缘的场地会使每次会议间隙的交流都变成一次出租车行程,而会议间隙的交流正是贸易峰会的主要目的所在。",
    "The conference programme on Days 1 and 2 runs inside the building.": "第1天和第2天的会议议程在建筑内进行。",
    "The tent": "帐篷",
    "The International Tea &amp; Technology Expo on Day 3 runs in a tent on the KICC\ngrounds rather than inside. 146 numbered stands across two halls, in a\n30m × 80m tent, with aisles of 3.0m and 2.0m.": "第3天的International Tea &amp; Technology Expo在KICC场地的帐篷内举行,而非室内。两个展厅共有146个编号展位,帐篷规格为30米×80米,通道宽度为3.0米和2.0米。",
    "This is worth stating plainly because an exhibitor who arrives expecting an\nindoor hall has a real problem on build day.": "需要明确说明这一点,因为期待室内展厅的参展商在布展当天会遇到实际问题。",
    "What a tented hall means if you are exhibiting": "如果您是参展商,帐篷式展厅意味着什么",
    "A tent gives a single uninterrupted floor with no columns, which produces\nbetter sightlines than most permanent halls. Sizes, rates and package\ninclusions are still being set, and the layout may change before stands go on\nsale.": "帐篷提供单一连续的无柱地面空间,比大多数永久性展厅产生更好的视线。规格、价格和套餐包含内容仍在制定中,展位开售前布局可能会有变化。",
    "Practical points to plan around once the exhibitor pack is published: power\ndistribution and lighting are specified per stand rather than assumed;\nflooring is laid rather than existing; and build and breakdown windows are\ntighter than in a permanent venue because the structure itself has a schedule.": "参展商手册发布后需要考虑的实际要点:每个展位的电力分配和照明是单独指定的,而非默认提供;地板是铺设的而非现有的;搭建和拆除时间窗口比永久性场馆更紧凑,因为结构本身有时间安排。",
    "Booking": "预订",
    "Register as an exhibitor and the Secretariat makes contact when rates are set\nand booking opens. Stands are then selected from an interactive plan in the\nexhibitor portal and held while the Secretariat confirms.": "注册为参展商后,秘书处会在价格确定并开放预订时与您联系。然后可以在参展商门户网站的交互式平面图中选择展位,并在秘书处确认期间保留。",
    "See <a href=\"/exhibition/stands/\">stands and rates</a> and the <a href=\"/venue/\">venue</a>.": "查看<a href=\"/exhibition/stands/\">展位和价格</a>以及<a href=\"/venue/\">场馆</a>。",
    "Six categories, from delegate to exhibitor. Fees and deadlines are published once the secretariat confirms them.": "六个类别,从代表到参展商。费用和截止日期将在秘书处确认后公布。",
